# enclosure.conf — paths and handle for tools/cu/cursor-jail.sh and launch-zed.sh.
#
# Copy to tools/e/enclosure.conf and fill in YOUR values. The real enclosure.conf
# is gitignored; only this .example is committed, so SOURCE.md and the spec
# work for anyone who clones the repo.
#
# See: context/specs/enclosure-editors.md

HANDLE="youruser"                          # forge handle; labels state dirs mentally
REPO="$HOME/yourrepo"                      # absolute path to the project root

# Editor binaries (adjust after install)
CURSOR_APPRUN="$REPO/squashfs-root/AppRun" # from: ./tools/cu/cursor-jail.sh --extract ./Cursor-3.9.16-x86_64.AppImage
ZED_BIN="zed"                              # optional hint; script also checks ~/.local/bin/zed
# ZED_APP="$HOME/.local/zed.app"           # optional; used if ZED_BIN is unset

# Project-local state (kept inside ai-jail's durable tree)
CURSOR_STATE="$REPO/.cursor-state"
ZED_STATE="$REPO/.zed-state"
# CLI agents (tools/ag/agent-jail.sh) -- gitignored; survive --private-home tmpfs HOME.
#
# LEFT UNSET ON PURPOSE (REDS %327). agent-jail.sh seats the one-room loop-state house
# itself -- $REPO/loops/claude, /cursor, /codex, seated 20260827 -- and adopts an elder
# .claude-state or .cursor-agent-state into it on the next launch. THIS FILE IS SOURCED
# BEFORE those defaults, so a path named here outranks the move: the elder is emptied by
# the adoption, recreated by `mkdir -p`, and bound over the agent's HOME with nothing in
# it, which asks for a login this launcher promises is done once per pier. Measured on the
# Framework pier 20260828: loops/claude held 5,229 files including .credentials.json while
# .claude-state held none. Uncomment one only to point somewhere the launcher cannot know.
# CLAUDE_STATE="$REPO/loops/claude"
# CURSOR_AGENT_STATE="$REPO/loops/cursor"
# CODEX_STATE="$REPO/loops/codex"
# cursor-agent OAuth (auth.json) -- defaults to $CURSOR_AGENT_STATE/xdg-config
# CURSOR_CONFIG_STATE="$REPO/loops/cursor/xdg-config"
GH_STATE="$REPO/.gh"
# $CLAUDE_STATE/dot-claude.json is SEEDED by the launcher and mounted onto ~/.claude.json, where
# Claude Code keeps hasCompletedOnboarding and the chosen theme. Nothing to copy by hand: this
# line used to say `optional`, which described a workaround for REDS %408 rather than a setting.

# ai-jail flags (space-separated). v1.20.2 defaults network off; CLI agents
# need --network to reach their APIs. --no-network wins if you set it.
AIJAIL_FLAGS="--private-home --no-docker --no-gpu --network"
# Headless pier / CLI agents already include --no-gpu above.
# AIJAIL_FLAGS="--private-home --no-docker --no-gpu --network"
# AIJAIL_BIN="/home/youruser/.local/bin/ai-jail"  # optional; avoids ./ai-jail source dir on PATH
# Preferred pin (gitignored cache — survives jail $HOME reset):
#   mkdir -p tools/.cache/bin && cd tools/.cache/bin
#   curl -fsSLO https://github.com/akitaonrails/ai-jail/releases/download/v1.12.0/ai-jail-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
#   echo "91458f153c7b0a87d79aae9014b558a0cfc4b160b7e390008a00c1adfc3edc21  ai-jail-linux-x86_64.tar.gz" | sha256sum -c -
#   tar -xzf ai-jail-linux-x86_64.tar.gz && rm ai-jail-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
# AIJAIL_BIN="$REPO/tools/.cache/bin/ai-jail"   # seated v1.12.0 · Claude pin 20260712.131200
# NixOS: a bare GitHub tarball hits stub-ld. The living overlay patchelfs
# v1.20.2 and wraps BWRAP_BIN. Standing door after rebuild-outer:
#   /run/current-system/sw/bin/ai-jail
# Leave AIJAIL_BIN unset so command -v finds that path. A store pin goes stale.
# Also keep empty /opt (bwrap ro-bind): systemd.tmpfiles.rules = [ "d /opt 0755 root root -" ];

# Zed on GNOME Wayland needs GPU passthrough (/dev/dri). Cursor can stay false.
# Keeper pier (headless): USE_GPU=false
USE_GPU=true

# KVM device lane (counsel 20260712.090512 A-narrow). Off by default.
# When true, tools/l/lane_kvm.sh authorizes /dev/kvm only — no D-Bus, no systemd
# host escapes, no session buses. Teacher ai-jail stays unmodified. Proven-seat
# on-path: tools/p/proven_seat_g0_complete_jailed.rish; refuse: lane_kvm_refuse.rish.
# One-shot from a host that already has /dev/kvm: tools/r/run_with_lane_kvm.sh
# One-shot without editing conf (caller export wins over this file):
#   LANE_KVM=true ./tools/r/run_with_lane_kvm.sh -- ./tools/p/proven_seat_g0c_lane_kvm.sh
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/lane_kvm_onpath_host.rish
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/lane_kvm_onpath_host.rish --parity
LANE_KVM=false

# Enclosure selector (Claude 212412 retreat · 213600 master-seal).
# Default ai-jail. Flip to pond only after bron-resins/pond-supersede-exit.bron
# is present-with-content AND master-signed (.bron.asc · fpr 0646 2132…).
# Helper: tools/p/pond_exit_bron_master_seal.sh. Both ENCLOSURE values stay live
# one full season past the flip.
ENCLOSURE=ai-jail

# Anthropic API key for Zed's Claude Agent — copy and fill in (gitignored):
#   cp tools/s/secrets.env.example tools/secrets.env
# launch-zed.sh sources tools/secrets.env automatically.
# Or export in your shell before launch (does not persist across terminals).
